  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rwanda National Tuberculosis Control Strategic Plan 2009-2012 - Rwanda (01-Jul-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Largely due to the HIV epidemic in Rwanda, the total number of TB cases nearly tripled from 159 cases per 100,000 in 1990 to 397 cases per 100,000 in 2006. Similarly, the number of new smear-positive cases was estimated to have nearly tripled from 62 cases per 100,000 in 1990 to 161 cases per 100,000 in 2006. The program supported by this grant aims to further reduce TB-related illness and death in Rwanda and reach the Millennium Development Goals by increasing TB and multidrug-resistant TB (MDR-TB) case detection; maintaining the high treatment success rate for TB and MDR-TB; decreasing TB and HIV/TB co-infection death rates; and strengthening Rwanda&amp;#39;s health system. The program targets TB patients treated under DOTS, people living with HIV, prisoners, and women and children.</narrative>
  </description>
